# An allowlist: ignore everything, then opt in what we actually track, so a
# new tool's files are excluded by default rather than caught retroactively
# (gcloud, gh and herdr all had to be). ~/.config is now an ordinary
# directory with individual files linked in, so this is a safety net rather
# than the primary defence -- but keep it that way.
#
# Adding a file: add a `!` line for it below. For a directory whose contents
# are all ours, `!/dir/` is enough. For a directory that also collects state,
# re-ignore its contents and opt in individual files -- see gh/ below.

/*
!/.gitignore
!/README.md

# --- nix ---------------------------------------------------------------------
!/flake.nix
!/flake.lock
!/configuration.nix
!/rebuild.sh
!/home-manager/

# --- XDG app configs ---------------------------------------------------------
# Linked into ~/.config by home-manager.
!/starship.toml
!/ghostty/
!/nvim/
!/zsh/
!/git/

# gh writes oauth tokens into hosts.yml, so opt in only config.yml.
!/gh/
/gh/*
!/gh/config.yml

# --- overrides ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Listed last so they win over any opt-in above.

# Credentials, wherever they turn up.
**/application_default_credentials.json
**/credentials.db
**/access_tokens.db
**/legacy_credentials/
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# home-manager activation backups.
*.hm-bak

# macOS / nix build output.
.DS_Store
result
result-*
